package dev.kb896.aiusage.rear

/**
 * Panel icons, as pixel rectangles.
 *
 * GENERATED by tools/trace-glyphs.py — do not edit by hand.
 *
 * Traced from the same Terminess Nerd Font glyphs the author's status bar uses, so
 * the panel matches the rest of the setup. Traced rather than bundled: shipping the
 * font to draw two glyphs would add megabytes to a 1.4MB release for shapes that are
 * a few dozen rectangles at this size, and every other mark on this panel is already
 * drawn that way.
 *
 * Coordinates are normalised 0..1 within the glyph's own bounding box, so a caller
 * picks a height and the icon fits it.
 */
object PanelIcons {

    /** x, y, w, h — all 0..1 of the icon's box. */
    class Rect(val x: Float, val y: Float, val w: Float, val h: Float)

    /**
     * An icon and the shape of its own box, together.
     *
     * Together deliberately. These used to be a list of rects and a separate
     * _ASPECT constant, which meant the drawing code had to pair them up by hand —
     * it did so with an if-chain that defaulted to the BATTERY aspect, so the first
     * icon added after that code was written was silently drawn battery-shaped:
     * tall and narrow, on a camera. A pair that must not be separated should not be
     * separable.
     */
    class Icon(val aspect: Float, val rects: List<Rect>)

